   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict all-incident reporting with a 72-hour regulator deadline and 24-hour customer notice, but no phase-in. S2 keeps a 55 °C test and a 5% safety-action trigger without automatic sales stop, gives results to customers but not the public, and is weakened by the lack of any mandatory sales stop. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and a six-year retrofit with an alternative risk-mitigation pathway; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months with regulator-approved equivalents; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k unless the regulator approves an unbounded alternative protective action, with prompt notices."
 },
